PRP-Graph (Luo et al., ACL 2024, https://aclanthology.org/2024.acl-long.313/), Section 2 / Figure 2(a), and its released code rankers/rank_flan.py (https://github.com/Memelank/PRP-Graph @ 968e45ee8178f5d3ac44a2b8f11f091af69206d7), which follows Qin et al. (2023) Pairwise Ranking Prompting. The paper's prompt is verbatim: 'Given a query "{query}", which of the following two passages is more relevant to the query?

Passage A:{doc1}

Passage B:{doc2}

Output Passage A or Passage B:'. The paper defines no labels beyond this prompt; the two options are its target labels 'Passage A' / 'Passage B' and their descriptions restate the prompt's question. PRP-Graph scores a comparison by the probability of 'Passage A' (Eq. 1); the adapter uses Jev's probability of the option 'Passage A'. Query (32 Flan-T5 tokens) and passages ('Title: ... Content: ...', 128 Flan-T5 tokens) are truncated as in rank_flan.py and supplied in the state under the keys below.
